              "variant": "scenario",
              "title": "What should Sahil do before Friday?",
              "scenario": "Sahil has the annexure above. He is in the new regime, pays ₹20,000 rent, wants to build savings for a flat in about 6 years, and is not sure he will stay at this company for more than 3 years. He has no dependants and a healthy personal budget of about ₹55,000 a month.",
              "prompt": "Which regime should he declare, what should he ask HR, and is there anything worth changing in the structure?",
              "modelAnswer": "Regime: new. His tax is nil in the new regime and ₹71,830 in the old, and he has ₹1,90,077 of room before any tax applies. Questions for HR: (1) actual bonus payout history, so he values the ₹60,000 realistically; (2) whether PF is on full basic and whether he can cap it; (3) sum insured on the medical policy; (4) whether the company plans a Labour Codes restructuring, and how basic, HRA and special allowance will change. Structure: there is no tax to save this year, so he should not waste effort on relabelling. Since he may leave before 5 years, he should mentally value gratuity at zero. Keeping PF on full basic is sensible given his flat goal: ₹1,15,200 a year goes into EPF on both sides, earning a tax-free rate, and his ₹80,410 in-hand comfortably covers his ₹55,000 budget. If a raise later pushes his taxable income towards ₹12,00,000, that is when meal vouchers, phone reimbursement and employer NPS become worth asking for.",
