            {
              "_type": "keyTakeaways",
              "points": [
                "Read any salary breakup in five passes: sort, strip, tax, deduct, stress-test.",
                "About 10% of Sahil's ₹12 lakh CTC never arrives as cash: meal card, insurance, employer PF and gratuity.",
                "At ₹12 lakh CTC with a meal card, new regime tax is nil, with ₹1,90,077 of room before tax starts.",
                "Monthly in-hand is ₹80,410, about 80% of CTC divided by 12.",
                "Always value variable pay at its real payout rate and gratuity at zero unless you expect to stay 5 years.",
                "Under the Labour Codes, special allowance counts as wages, so gratuity may be worth more than the CTC line shows."
